{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe `scanner-integration (pinned Semgrep + Gitleaks on the patchset)` job, added to `main` in\n`6125c5345f01` (Gerrit change 2595, ticket aa9e), fails on every change pushed since it merged.\nIt casts `Verified -1` and blocks all merges; six open changes are affected (2594, 2600, 2601,\n2607, 2608, 2609). With bug `9a17-e0b3-7aa6-4091` this leaves two gates red and no route to\n`Verified +1`.\n\n**How it landed broken (the escape).** The job never ran before merge. Change 2595's own\nVerified run `33831682168` contains 26 jobs and no `scanner-integration` job at all: the\nVerified lane executes `gerrit-verify.yaml` from trusted `main`, and `main` did not yet wire\nthe lane. So 2595's `Verified +1` was cast without the new job ever executing. Absence of\ncoverage, not divergent conditions — base staleness is ruled out (change 2607 is parented\ndirectly on `6125c5345f01` and still fails).\n\n**Why it fails (the fault) — two independent defects, both quoted from real job logs.**\n\nDefect 1, the make recipe is not POSIX-sh portable. On a tree that carries the new script\n(mirror branch-head lane, run 33834183836 job 100903189596, base `main`):\n\n```\nreview scanner locks: OK\n/bin/sh: 1: set: Illegal option -o pipefail\nmake: *** [Makefile:475: scanner-integration] Error 2\n```\n\n`Makefile:475` opens the recipe with `@set -euo pipefail;`. The Makefile sets no `SHELL`, so\nGNU make runs recipes under `/bin/sh` — dash on ubuntu-latest, which has no `pipefail`. The\nrecipe contains no pipeline, so `pipefail` buys nothing. This breaks the job on main content\nitself, independently of the patchset context.\n\nDefect 2, the gate step is unguarded against a pre-gate base. Change 2608 (patchset\n`f50dc100`, run 33837736047 job 100913937750):\n\n```\npython: can't open file '/home/runner/work/rebar/rebar/scripts/install_review_scanners.py':\n[Errno 2] No such file or directory\n```\n\n`.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml` runs `scripts/install_review_scanners.py` and\n`make scanner-integration` with no `[ -f ]` guard and no `# predates-gate-ok:` marker — the\nexact invariant `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` owns. That guard's\n`GUARDED_WORKFLOWS` is a hardcoded tuple; `_scanner-integration.yml` (like `_artifact-probe.yml`\nand `_eval-discipline.yml`) is wired into `gerrit-verify.yaml` but absent from the tuple, so the\ncompleteness check never looked at it. A new lane is opt-in to its own invariant, which is\nbackwards.\n\n## Approach\n\nThe pre-merge property to restore is that a newly added CI lane's correctness is enforced by\nthe **unit-test suite**, which always executes on the change that introduces it, rather than by\nthe new job, which does not. Both defects are made catchable that way, and the opt-in step that\n2595 could skip is removed.\n\n1. `Makefile` — replace `set -euo pipefail` with POSIX `set -eu` in the `scanner-integration`\n   recipe. The recipe has no pipeline, so this is behaviour-preserving under bash and correct\n   under dash.\n2. `.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml` — wrap the gate step in the canonical\n   `[ -f scripts/install_review_scanners.py ]` guard emitting the exact phrase\n   `change predates the gate`, and make the failure path actionable: name the violated contract\n   (pinned Semgrep + Gitleaks locks) and print the local reproduction command\n   `make scanner-integration`.\n3. `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` — derive `GUARDED_WORKFLOWS` from the lane\n   instead of hardcoding it: take `gerrit-verify.yaml` and `test.yml` as roots and follow every\n   local `uses: ./.github/...` reference transitively. A reusable workflow or composite action\n   is then inside the invariant the moment it is wired, with no second edit. Keep the current\n   tuple as an asserted floor so the derivation cannot silently shrink.\n4. `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` — pin defect 1's class: every make recipe reachable\n   from CI must parse under a strict POSIX shell, so a bash-only builtin fails in the local\n   suite instead of on ubuntu-latest.\n\nNo new script, config key, env var, feature flag or lock is introduced, so the mechanism-delta\nratchet sees no new mechanism.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `Makefile` — the `scanner-integration` recipe's `set` line.\n- `.github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml` — guard plus actionable failure message.\n- `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` — lane-derived guarded set, coverage assertion.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` — POSIX-shell contract for make recipes.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: the scanner step is inside `test_completeness_every_gate_step_is_guarded_or_marked`\n  and `test_empty_tree_every_guarded_step_skips_cleanly`; the guarded body run in an empty\n  directory exits 0 and prints `change predates the gate`.\n- Coverage path: a new assertion pins that the derived guarded set contains every local `uses:`\n  target reachable from `gerrit-verify.yaml` and `test.yml`, so a future lane cannot be wired\n  outside the invariant.\n- Failure/edge path (defect-seeded RED): reintroduce each fault — drop the `-f` guard, and\n  restore `set -euo pipefail` — and show the corresponding test fail, then revert.\n- Empty/degenerate path: a recipe with no shell content passes the POSIX parse trivially rather\n  than erroring.\n- Verification set: `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and\n  `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py -q`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Root cause is quoted from real job logs, not inferred from workflow source: both the\n      `Illegal option -o pipefail` failure (job 100903189596) and the `No such file or\n      directory` failure (job 100913937750) are cited with job ids. Checked by reading this\n      description and the change's commit message.\n- [ ] `scanner-integration` passes on a patchset that is otherwise unmodified relative to its\n      base. Checked by this fix's Gerrit change reaching `Verified +1` with the\n      `scanner-integration` job green.\n- [ ] The escape is closed: a newly added CI lane can no longer land unvalidated because its own\n      job did not execute on the introducing change. `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py`\n      derives its workflow set from the `gerrit-verify.yaml`/`test.yml` local-`uses:` closure\n      rather than a hardcoded list, so the always-running unit suite covers a lane the moment it\n      is wired; the make-recipe POSIX contract covers defect 1 the same way. Checked by running\n      both modules and by the new coverage assertion failing when a lane member is omitted.\n- [ ] Defect-seeded RED: with the guard removed the completeness test fails naming\n      `_scanner-integration.yml`, and with `set -euo pipefail` restored the POSIX contract fails\n      naming `scanner-integration`; both pass after revert. Checked by the quoted pytest output\n      recorded in a ticket comment.\n- [ ] The job's failure message names the violated contract and the local command that\n      reproduces it. Checked by reading the step body: the failure path prints\n      `make scanner-integration` as the local reproduction."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788499232120134001,"uuid":"45368299-30f6-47bd-b1b0-162cc1659a21"}